    "rawCopy": "Marketing celebrates hitting 120% of MQL quota. Sales hits 65% of revenue quota. Who is right?\n\nNeither. The business lost.\n\nThis recurring friction is the direct consequence of disjointed incentives:\n- Marketing is evaluated on top-of-funnel volume: form submissions, webinar signups, and eBook downloads.\n- Sales is evaluated on booked annual recurring revenue and commercial cash collection.\n- Customer Success is left holding the bag when low-fit customers churn after 9 months.\n\nWhen departments operate with separate scorecards, each team optimizes its own operational comfort while the enterprise as a whole leaks capital.\n\nIn an AI-Native Revenue Transformation, demand generation and sales execution merge into a single continuous workflow:\n\n1. Unified ICP Scorecards: Marketing is only credited for pipeline that meets verified commercial qualification criteria.\n2. Shared Revenue Quotas: Marketing leadership shares pipeline conversion and closed-won revenue accountability with sales.\n3. Closed-Loop Telemetry: Sales outcome data immediately feeds back into top-of-funnel targeting, automatically suppressing segments that stall or demand heavy discounts.\n\nStop running two separate go-to-market teams. Build one integrated revenue engine.\n\n#GTMAlignment #RevenueOperations #MarketingAndSales #CRO #B2BLeadership",
