    "idFormatted": "011",
    "title": "Diagnosing conversion losses",
    "category": "Conversion Optimization",
    "subcategory": "Deal Execution & Qualification",
    "format": "single-image",
    "targetAudience": "B2B Revenue Leaders & Commercial Executives",
    "contentBrief": "Explain how to locate the stages where qualified opportunities fail to progress and how to investigate the reasons behind those losses.",
    "mdPath": "single-image/conversion-optimization/011-diagnosing-conversion-losses.md",
    "htmlPath": "single-image/conversion-optimization/011-diagnosing-conversion-losses.html",
    "imagePath": "assets/post-images/011-diagnosing-conversion-losses.png",
    "imageFilename": "011-diagnosing-conversion-losses.png",
    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "When an enterprise deal is marked 'Closed Lost' in the CRM, 70% of reps write down: 'Lost to competitor' or 'Lost on price.'\n\nIn reality, price is almost never the real reason.\n\nExtensive commercial post-mortems reveal that conversion losses occur because of systemic execution gaps earlier in the sales cycle:\n\n1. Post-Discovery Drop-Off: The prospect goes silent because the rep pitched features before the prospect agreed on the quantified cost of doing nothing.\n2. Post-Demonstration Stall: The buyer says 'this looks great, let me socialize it internally'—a polite signal that you failed to provide a defensible business case for the CFO.\n3. Severe Price Resistance: The buyer aggressively demands a 30% discount because the proposal reads like a technical spec rather than a strategic business transformation.\n4. Late-Stage Procurement Veto: InfoSec or procurement halts the deal because the rep failed to engage legal and compliance stakeholders early.\n\nStop accepting 'timing' as an excuse for lost deals. Treat conversion losses as diagnostic signals that reveal exactly where your sales methodology needs re-engineering.\n\nWhat is the single biggest stage where your deals stall?\n\n#SalesExecution #ConversionOptimization #DealWinRate #RevOps #SalesStrategy",
