    "rawCopy": "If you pitch software features to an executive, they will evaluate you as an expense.\n\nIf you connect their operational bottlenecks to balance sheet impact, they will evaluate you as a high-yield strategic investment.\n\nThe biggest mistake B2B sales teams make is stopping at Level 1 pain:\n- The user tells the rep: 'Our CRM data is disorganized and manual updates take too much time.'\n- The rep immediately demos their automated workflow features.\n- The CFO rejects the purchase order because 'improving data entry' is not a top-three strategic board objective.\n\nTo win enterprise deals, you must cross the Problem-to-Value Bridge:\n\n1. Functional Pain: Manual data logging and fragmented account research.\n2. Operational Bottleneck: Sales development velocity is constrained; response latency averages 6 hours.\n3. Commercial Consequence: Inbound conversion decays by 40%, generating $1.2M in annual pipeline leakage.\n4. Executive Outcome: Quota attainment drops, CAC increases by 25%, and EBITDA margins contract.\n\nNow the conversation is not about software seats. It is about recovering $1.2M in leaked revenue and expanding enterprise margins.\n\nWhich level of value is your sales team pitching today?\n\n#ValueSelling #EnterpriseSales #B2BStrategy #CommercialExcellence #CRO",
