    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "B2B buyers do not hate buying. They hate the friction vendor sales processes force them to endure.\n\nConsider the typical enterprise buyer journey:\n- They fill out a 15-field form on your website.\n- An SDR calls them 24 hours later to ask the exact same questions they just typed into the form.\n- They are transferred to an AE who makes them repeat their business challenges from scratch.\n- The AE refuses to discuss pricing until the third meeting.\n- Procurement and legal are surprised by non-standard contracts in week twelve.\n\nEvery friction point gives your buyer an opportunity to pause, re-evaluate, or do nothing.\n\nModern AI-Native revenue teams treat buying friction as an existential revenue leak:\n- Automated enrichment replaces long inquiry forms.\n- Synchronized account dossiers ensure no prospect ever repeats their story twice.\n- Transparent value modeling provides clear commercial expectations early.\n- Pre-packaged InfoSec and compliance documentation speeds legal approval.\n\nMake it frictionless for qualified buyers to buy from you.\n\nWhere is the biggest friction point in your current sales journey?\n\n#BuyingJourney #CustomerExperience #B2BSales #DealVelocity #RevOps",
