    "imagePath": "assets/post-images/016-understanding-stalled-deals.png",
    "imageFilename": "016-understanding-stalled-deals.png",
    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "A stalled deal is not a neutral asset in your CRM. It is an active drain on your sales capacity.\n\nEvery week an account executive spends preparing follow-up emails, forecasting close dates, and agonizing over an unresponsive prospect is time stolen from active opportunities:\n\nWhen deals stall, there are only four real causes:\n\n1. Lack of Economic Buyer Alignment: Your champion is excited, but they lack the budget authority to sign a purchase order without CFO sign-off.\n2. The Business Case Is Too Weak: The problem was framed as an operational convenience rather than an urgent financial necessity.\n3. Internal Political Resistance: Another internal department views your platform as a threat to their budget or headcount.\n4. Ghost Pipeline: The prospect has chosen another vendor or decided to do nothing, but avoids telling you to avoid conflict.\n\nApply strict triage rules: If an opportunity fails to provide verified buyer actions for 30 days, send a respectful close-out notice and re-allocate rep capacity to high-momentum accounts.\n\nCleaning dead deals out of your pipeline is the fastest way to increase real sales velocity.\n\nHow many 'zombie deals' are currently inflating your quarterly forecast?\n\n#SalesLeadership #PipelineTriage #SalesStrategy #B2BRevenue #RevOps",
    "cleanCopy": "A stalled deal is not a neutral asset in your CRM. It is an active drain on your sales capacity.\n\nEvery week an account executive spends preparing follow-up emails, forecasting close dates, and agonizing over an unresponsive prospect is time stolen from active opportunities:\n\nWhen deals stall, there are only four real causes:\n\n1. Lack of Economic Buyer Alignment: Your champion is excited, but they lack the budget authority to sign a purchase order without CFO sign-off.\n2. The Business Case Is Too Weak: The problem was framed as an operational convenience rather than an urgent financial necessity.\n3. Internal Political Resistance: Another internal department views your platform as a threat to their budget or headcount.\n4. Ghost Pipeline: The prospect has chosen another vendor or decided to do nothing, but avoids telling you to avoid conflict.\n\nApply strict triage rules: If an opportunity fails to provide verified buyer actions for 30 days, send a respectful close-out notice and re-allocate rep capacity to high-momentum accounts.\n\nCleaning dead deals out of your pipeline is the fastest way to increase real sales velocity.\n\nHow many 'zombie deals' are currently inflating your quarterly forecast?",
