    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "The 15 minutes immediately following a sales call determine whether that opportunity progresses or evaporates.\n\nWhat typically happens after an AE hangs up a Zoom call?\n- They immediately jump into the next scheduled meeting.\n- Important nuances, unaddressed buyer objections, and committed next steps fade from memory.\n- By Friday afternoon, they rush through their CRM typing: 'Good call. Demo went well. Following up next week.'\n\nThis is how deals slip through the cracks.\n\nHigh-velocity commercial engines deploy an automated post-call debriefing loop:\n\n1. Autonomous Transcription & Extraction: The conversation is instantly analyzed to extract validated customer pain points, mentioned competitors, agreed deadlines, and committed deliverables.\n2. Draft Follow-Up Generation: The seller receives a pre-drafted, tailored executive follow-up email in their inbox within 3 minutes of call completion—requiring only quick human review before sending.\n3. Instant CRM Synchronization: Stage criteria, pipeline value, next action dates, and objection tags are automatically updated in the CRM without the seller clicking a single dropdown.\n\nWhen post-call momentum is captured immediately, buyer responsiveness surges and CRM hygiene reaches near 100%.\n\nHow much crucial deal context does your team lose between meetings?\n\n#SalesExecution #CRMHygiene #SalesCoaching #RevOps #SalesProductivity",
