    "imageFilename": null,
    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "Most sales managers spend 80% of their 1-on-1s asking reps for pipeline status updates instead of coaching commercial skills.\n\nThe typical weekly check-in is an administrative interrogation:\n- 'What's happening with the Acme Corp deal?'\n- 'Did you send the contract to GlobalTech?'\n- 'Why did this deal push into next month?'\n\nBy the time the manager gets through the CRM pipeline inspect, the 30-minute meeting is over. Zero coaching took place.\n\nAI-assisted sales management flips this dynamic completely:\n\n1. Autonomous Telemetry Analysis: Conversation intelligence platforms automatically analyze talk-to-listen ratios, objection handling efficacy, and whether reps are qualifying economic buyer access.\n2. Skill Gap Heatmaps: Managers receive weekly summaries identifying systemic weaknesses across the team (e.g., 'Rep A excels at discovery but struggles to navigate pricing resistance at proposal stage').\n3. High-Leverage Coaching 1-on-1s: Because deal status is already transparent in the CRM telemetry, the entire meeting is dedicated to role-playing, objection navigation, and deal strategy.\n\nWhen coaching is grounded in objective behavioral data, rep ramp times drop by 40% and quota attainment becomes a repeatable science across the entire team.\n\nAre your sales managers coaching behaviors or interrogating spreadsheets?\n\n#SalesCoaching #SalesLeadership #RevenueEnablement #RevOps #SalesManagement",
