    "imagePath": null,
    "imageFilename": null,
    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "The fastest way to turn an 80% software margin into a 35% services margin is 'unlimited onboarding support.'\n\nDuring high-stakes enterprise sales cycles, reps frequently make verbal concessions to push contracts over the finish line:\n- 'Don't worry, our team will help you build all the custom dashboard reports.'\n- 'We will handle the data migration from your legacy database free of charge.'\n- 'Our solutions engineers will write the custom API scripts for you.'\n\nWhen the contract is signed:\n- Customer Success inherits dozens of undocumented commitments.\n- Onboarding timeline stretches from 30 days to 6 months.\n- High-priced engineers spend hundreds of hours doing bespoke services work that was never factored into the commercial model.\n\nScope creep is a systemic failure of commercial governance:\n\n1. Pre-Engineered SOW Guardrails: Statements of Work must feature explicit boundary clauses detailing exactly what is included and what constitutes a billable change order.\n2. Modular Implementation Packages: Standardize onboarding into fixed tiers (e.g., Core vs Enterprise Guided) with predefined milestone deliverables.\n3. Commercial Accountability for Sales: If an account executive commits bespoke engineering hours to win a deal, the cost of those hours must be debited against their deal commission.\n\nProtect your delivery teams from open-ended promises. Standardize your scope to protect your gross margin.\n\nHow often does your professional services team absorb unbilled work to keep a new customer happy?\n\n#ScopeCreep #GrossMargin #ProfessionalServices #CustomerSuccess #RevOps",
