    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "Per-seat pricing is actively killing B2B software expansion.\n\nWhen you charge strictly per user seat:\n- Your customers share passwords to avoid buying additional licenses.\n- Department heads restrict user access to cut software costs.\n- You actively penalize the customer for adopting your platform across their enterprise.\n\nModern pricing architecture aligns the commercial contract with customer value realization:\n\n1. Flawed Legacy Model (Per-Seat): Creates artificial friction. The customer's financial incentive is to limit platform usage, directly contradicting their success.\n2. Pure Usage Model (Unpredictable): Highly variable bills make enterprise budgeting difficult for CFOs, creating quarterly billing friction.\n3. Hybrid Platform Model (Optimal): A predictable annual platform base fee that covers core enterprise capabilities, paired with transparent tiered value metrics (e.g., pipeline volume analyzed, records enriched, transactions processed).\n\nWhen your pricing expands naturally as the customer gets more business value, account expansion requires zero friction.\n\nDoes your current pricing model incentivize customers to expand usage or restrict it?\n\n#PricingStrategy #B2BCommerce #GrossMargin #SaaSArchitecture #RevOps",
    "cleanCopy": "Per-seat pricing is actively killing B2B software expansion.\n\nWhen you charge strictly per user seat:\n- Your customers share passwords to avoid buying additional licenses.\n- Department heads restrict user access to cut software costs.\n- You actively penalize the customer for adopting your platform across their enterprise.\n\nModern pricing architecture aligns the commercial contract with customer value realization:\n\n1. Flawed Legacy Model (Per-Seat): Creates artificial friction. The customer's financial incentive is to limit platform usage, directly contradicting their success.\n2. Pure Usage Model (Unpredictable): Highly variable bills make enterprise budgeting difficult for CFOs, creating quarterly billing friction.\n3. Hybrid Platform Model (Optimal): A predictable annual platform base fee that covers core enterprise capabilities, paired with transparent tiered value metrics (e.g., pipeline volume analyzed, records enriched, transactions processed).\n\nWhen your pricing expands naturally as the customer gets more business value, account expansion requires zero friction.\n\nDoes your current pricing model incentivize customers to expand usage or restrict it?",
