    "imagePath": null,
    "imageFilename": null,
    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "Carrying 100 dead opportunities in your CRM isn't harmless optimism. It is an active financial drain on quota capacity.\n\nEvery sales organization has a pipeline graveyard:\n- Opportunities that haven't answered an email in 45 days.\n- Prospects who said 'check back with us next quarter' six months ago.\n- Deals where the champion left the company, but the rep refuses to mark it closed-lost.\n\nReps hold onto bad pipeline because an empty pipeline feels terrifying.\n\nBut the opportunity cost is devastating:\n- Every hour spent preparing follow-up emails for a dead prospect is an hour stolen from finding active, high-intent buyers.\n- Managers waste 30% of weekly pipeline inspections debating fictional opportunities.\n- Executive forecasts become unmoored from reality, leading to surprise revenue misses at quarter-end.\n\nRuthless disqualification is a superpower of high-performing revenue engines:\n- If a prospect refuses to introduce the economic buyer after two meetings, disqualify.\n- If there is no agreed deadline driving action in the next 90 days, disqualify.\n- If the customer does not have the technical infrastructure to succeed with your product, disqualify.\n\nDisqualifying bad pipeline on Day 14 doesn't hurt your quota. It liberates your time to close high-yield deals on Day 45.\n\nPurge the ghost pipeline from your CRM.\n\nWhat percentage of your active opportunities took a verified buyer action in the last 7 days?\n\n#OpportunityCost #PipelineHygiene #SalesDiscipline #SalesExecution #RevOps",
