    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "If your blended company win rate is 22%, that average is lying to you.\n\nWhen you deconstruct win rates by contract size and customer segment, clear patterns emerge:\n- You might have a 45% win rate in mid-market accounts with 100–500 employees.\n- And an 8% win rate in Fortune 500 enterprise accounts requiring bespoke compliance.\n\nYet where do most executive teams push their sales reps?\nStraight into the Fortune 500 trap—where reps spend 9 months chasing mega-deals that have a 90% chance of failing.\n\nTo build an efficient revenue engine, you must map your Commercial Power Alley:\n\n1. The Power Alley: Where win rates exceed 35%, sales cycles close in under 60 days, and gross margins remain above 80%. This is your core economic growth engine.\n2. The Expansion Zone: High-potential segments that require minor packaging and scoping refinements to reach power alley efficiency.\n3. The Distraction Trap: Massive logos with low win rates, endless procurement friction, and heavy custom engineering that drains operating capital.\n4. The Automated Tier: Low-ACV accounts that must be serviced via self-checkout rather than expensive human sales reps.\n\nAlign your sales capacity with where your product naturally wins.\n\nDo you know the exact boundary of your company's commercial power alley?\n\n#WinRate #GTMStrategy #SalesAnalytics #PowerAlley #RevenueAcceleration",
    "cleanCopy": "If your blended company win rate is 22%, that average is lying to you.\n\nWhen you deconstruct win rates by contract size and customer segment, clear patterns emerge:\n- You might have a 45% win rate in mid-market accounts with 100–500 employees.\n- And an 8% win rate in Fortune 500 enterprise accounts requiring bespoke compliance.\n\nYet where do most executive teams push their sales reps?\nStraight into the Fortune 500 trap—where reps spend 9 months chasing mega-deals that have a 90% chance of failing.\n\nTo build an efficient revenue engine, you must map your Commercial Power Alley:\n\n1. The Power Alley: Where win rates exceed 35%, sales cycles close in under 60 days, and gross margins remain above 80%. This is your core economic growth engine.\n2. The Expansion Zone: High-potential segments that require minor packaging and scoping refinements to reach power alley efficiency.\n3. The Distraction Trap: Massive logos with low win rates, endless procurement friction, and heavy custom engineering that drains operating capital.\n4. The Automated Tier: Low-ACV accounts that must be serviced via self-checkout rather than expensive human sales reps.\n\nAlign your sales capacity with where your product naturally wins.\n\nDo you know the exact boundary of your company's commercial power alley?",
