    "rawCopy": "Most executive revenue dashboards are completely useless.\n\nThey show beautiful, colorful charts that answer the question: 'What happened last month?'\n- Blue bars showing total lead volume.\n- Green lines showing closed ARR.\n- Pie charts showing deal distribution.\n\nLeaders look at them, nod politely, and then ask: 'So what do we actually do on Monday morning?'\n\nAn Action-Oriented Revenue Intelligence Dashboard does not report historical data. It diagnoses friction and prescribes commercial action:\n\n1. Stage Dwell Alerts: '14 enterprise deals have exceeded the 18-day median dwell time in Scoping. Mandate: Trigger technical scoping review.'\n2. Multi-Threading Telemetry: '65% of active Stage 3 opportunities lack verified contact with the economic buyer. Mandate: Require VP-level outreach before proposal dispatch.'\n3. Margin Dilution Monitor: 'Average sales discounting increased by 4% this month. Mandate: Enforce Tier-2 Deal Desk trade-off rules.'\n4. Expansion Opportunity Triggers: '8 key customer accounts hit 90% seat saturation this week. Mandate: Deploy automated tier upgrade proposals.'\n\nYour dashboard should not be a museum of past achievements. It should be an operating system that tells your team exactly where to intervene to protect revenue.\n\nDoes your current sales dashboard report history, or direct action?\n\n#RevenueIntelligence #ExecutiveDashboard #RevOps #SalesOperations #CRO",
