    "rawCopy": "Blasting an enterprise prospect with a rigid 8-step generic email sequence is the fastest way to get marked as spam.\n\nStatic cadence tools treat every prospect like an automated recipient:\n- If the prospect forwards your email to their CFO, the sequence doesn't know. It sends a generic 'Did you see my last email?' two days later.\n- If the prospect downloads your security whitepaper, the tool sends an introductory high-level video.\n\nModern commercial engines deploy Dynamic Adaptive Cadences:\n\nThe Adaptive Follow-Up Loop:\n1. Touch 1: Tailored executive summary delivered within 60 minutes of call completion.\n2. Behavioral Branching:\n   - If Forwarded Internally -> System alerts the rep: 'Champion forwarded proposal to VP Finance.' The next message dynamically provides an executive ROI spreadsheet.\n   - If Unopened After 48 Hours -> System shifts tone, offering a low-friction diagnostic insight rather than a pushy follow-up.\n   - If Security Doc Viewed -> System automatically provides pre-approved SOC2 compliance credentials to the InfoSec lead.\n\nYour follow-ups should respond to the buyer's internal behavior, not an arbitrary automated timer.\n\nHow adaptive is your sales team's current follow-up cadence?\n\n#SalesSequencing #EmailOutreach #AdaptiveSales #RevOps #SalesAcceleration",
