    "rawCopy": "The single biggest complaint new enterprise customers have is: 'Why do I have to re-explain my business to your onboarding team?'\n\nThink about the buyer's experience:\n- They spent 3 months in detailed discovery and technical demos with your sales team.\n- They explained their corporate goals, their internal bottlenecks, and their IT requirements.\n- The contract is signed.\n- Two weeks later, a Customer Success Manager jumps on a kickoff call and asks: 'So, tell me what you're hoping to achieve with our platform.'\n\nIn that single moment, the customer's confidence in your organization plummets.\n\nAutonomous Post-Sale Handoffs eliminate internal amnesia:\n\nThe Connected Handoff Architecture:\n1. Automated Dossier Synthesis: The moment the contract is signed in DocuSign, autonomous intelligence parses all recorded sales calls, discovery notes, and technical scoping documents.\n2. Customer Success Onboarding Charter: Generates a tailored 90-day onboarding charter detailing:\n   - The customer's primary economic objectives and validated P&L metrics.\n   - Key internal stakeholders, champions, and potential skeptics.\n   - Identified IT and integration dependencies.\n3. Contextual First Kickoff: The CSM enters the kickoff call already fully briefed: 'We know your top priority is reducing response latency by Q3. Here is our exact 30-day plan to deliver that outcome.'\n\nWhen your post-sale team operates with seamless context, customer time-to-value accelerates and renewals become guaranteed.\n\nHow much sales context does your customer success team actually receive after a deal closes?\n\n#CustomerSuccess #CustomerOnboarding #Handoffs #RevOps #NetRevenueRetention",
