    "rawCopy": "Building an AI-native sales organization does not mean buying 10 random AI plugins and hoping for the best.\n\nBolting generative AI tools onto a broken legacy process only creates faster chaos:\n- Unvetted automated messages hallucinate non-standard pricing.\n- Fragmented tools create new data silos.\n- Reps spend their day managing prompts instead of talking to buyers.\n\nA true AI-Native Sales Architecture is engineered across four integrated layers:\n\n1. Trust, Security & Governance Foundation: Enterprise SOC2 compliance, automated PII data masking, and mandatory human-in-the-loop approval gates.\n2. Unified Telemetry Spine: Single source of truth that ingests dark intent, validates contact data, and auto-syncs CRM records without rep effort.\n3. AI Co-Piloting Engine: Contextual intelligence that synthesizes 360° account dossiers, delivers in-flight battlecards, and monitors deal slippage risk.\n4. Commercial Workflow Layer: Equipping frontline sellers to execute high-impact discovery, consultative business cases, and frictionless handoffs.\n\nThis is systems engineering for revenue generation.\n\nIs your sales technology a collection of disconnected tools, or an integrated enterprise architecture?\n\n#SalesArchitecture #EnterpriseAI #RevOps #SalesTechnology #CRO",
