    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "When board members only ask: 'Did we hit the ARR number this quarter?', they fail to see the structural risks developing inside the enterprise.\n\nA company can hit its quarterly ARR target while its commercial engine is actively breaking down:\n- The target was achieved only because the CEO stepped in to close a single massive deal at a 40% discount.\n- Meanwhile, 80% of frontline reps missed their quotas.\n- Pipeline generation for next quarter dried up.\n- CAC increased by 35%, and gross margins collapsed.\n\nTo provide real corporate governance, board members must inspect five structural revenue health metrics:\n\nThe Boardroom Revenue Scorecard:\n1. Pipeline Coverage Density: Ratio of rigorously qualified pipeline to target quota (Target: 3.0x to 3.5x verified coverage).\n2. Frontline Capacity Attainment: Percentage of reps meeting target (Target: 70%+ across the entire team).\n3. CAC Payback Velocity: Speed of cash-flow recovery (Target: Sub-12 months on a gross-profit basis).\n4. Net Contract Gross Margin: True contract profitability after factoring in discounting and custom delivery (Target: 80%+).\n5. Forecast Variance: Discrepancy between executive commit and closed revenue (Target: Under 5%).\n\nWhen boards inspect systems rather than celebrating lucky outcomes, revenue predictability compounds.\n\nWhat metrics does your board inspect during quarterly commercial reviews?\n\n#BoardOfDirectors #Governance #CEO #RevenuePredictability #PrivateEquity",
