    "rawCopy": "Why do Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success spend half their executive syncs blaming one another?\n\nBecause they are incentivized on competing metrics:\n- Marketing is evaluated on MQLs: So they flood the CRM with downloadable eBooks and webinar signups.\n- Sales is evaluated on Booked ARR: So reps hand out 30% discounts and promise custom features just to hit their quarterly quota.\n- Customer Success is evaluated on Retention: So they inherit discounted, mis-qualified accounts that demand custom engineering and churn in Month 9.\n\nWhen each team hits its individual goal, the business can still burn cash.\n\nHigh-velocity CROs replace fragmented KPIs with a single overarching commercial metric:\n\nNet Profitable ARR Yield:\n(Qualified ICP Pipeline × Commercial Win Rate % × Gross Margin Contribution %) - Fully Loaded CAC\n\nUnder this unified model:\n- Marketing is only credited for pipeline that meets verified ICP criteria and advances to proposal.\n- Sales commission accelerates on contracts that maintain gross margin and cash-flow terms.\n- Customer Success feeds real product adoption telemetry back into top-of-funnel targeting.\n\nOne metric. One score. Complete commercial alignment.\n\nWhat primary metric aligns your marketing, sales, and retention teams today?\n\n#GTMAlignment #CRO #RevenueOperations #NorthStarMetric #CommercialStrategy",
