    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "If your sales team has a software tool for every day of the week, your GTM budget is leaking hundreds of thousands of dollars.\n\nDuring the zero-interest-rate boom, software budgets were completely ungoverned:\n- Sales managers put niche tools on corporate credit cards.\n- Marketing bought dedicated analytics suites that were abandoned after 60 days.\n- Today, the average enterprise GTM team uses 12 to 16 distinct software platforms, costing $1,200 to $1,800 per rep per month.\n\nThe CFO's mandate is to enforce SaaS Stack Rationalization:\n\n1. Zero-Based Software Auditing: Require every software contract up for renewal to justify its existence based on verified rep adoption and direct revenue attribution. (If login rates are below 50%, terminate the contract).\n2. Eliminate Redundant Capabilities: Consolidate overlapping point solutions (e.g., separate tools for sequencing, conversation recording, and intent data) into a unified platform.\n3. Consolidate Seat Licensing: Move away from disconnected user licenses toward platform-wide enterprise agreements that reduce cost per employee by 40%+.\n\nCutting software sprawl doesn't just save money. It removes operational friction and lets your sellers focus on customer conversations.\n\nWhen was the last time your finance team audited user login rates across your sales tech stack?\n\n#SaaSManagement #ToolSprawl #CFO #CostOptimization #RevOps",
