    "htmlPath": "single-image/executive-perspectives/098-choosing-the-next-growth-constraint-to-solve.html",
    "imagePath": "assets/post-images/098-choosing-the-next-growth-constraint-to-solve.png",
    "imageFilename": "098-choosing-the-next-growth-constraint-to-solve.png",
    "imageExists": true,
    "mdExists": true,
    "rawCopy": "When a company isn't growing fast enough, founders often launch 10 disconnected initiatives simultaneously:\n- 'Let's redesign the website!'\n- 'Let's launch an outbound email campaign!'\n- 'Let's hire an outbound SDR agency!'\n- 'Let's build a new product feature!'\n\nThe team works 70 hours a week, but revenue doesn't move.\n\nWhy? Because according to the Theory of Constraints:\nIn any complex system, there is only ONE primary constraint limiting throughput at any given moment.\n\nOptimizing a non-constraint produces zero measurable results:\n- If your constraint is deal conversion at the proposal stage, generating 500 more marketing leads will not produce a single dollar of additional revenue. It will just waste rep time.\n- If your constraint is post-sale customer retention, doubling your sales headcount will only accelerate your churn rate.\n\nApply the Growth Constraint Triage:\n1. Demand Constraint: Are your reps' calendars under 50% booked with qualified buyers? -> Fix: Intent discovery and account selection.\n2. Conversion Constraint: Are qualified meetings failing to progress to proposal? -> Fix: Consultative discovery and problem-to-value translation.\n3. Velocity Constraint: Are deals stalling for 90+ days in procurement? -> Fix: Mutual Action Plans and pre-cleared legal packs.\n4. Retention Constraint: Are customers churning after Year 1? -> Fix: Delivery standardization and time-to-value acceleration.\n\nFind your single primary bottleneck. Focus 100% of your executive energy on solving it.\n\nWhat is the single biggest constraint limiting your revenue growth today?\n\n#GrowthStrategy #TheoryOfConstraints #Founders #SalesOperations #RevOps",
    "cleanCopy": "When a company isn't growing fast enough, founders often launch 10 disconnected initiatives simultaneously:\n- 'Let's redesign the website!'\n- 'Let's launch an outbound email campaign!'\n- 'Let's hire an outbound SDR agency!'\n- 'Let's build a new product feature!'\n\nThe team works 70 hours a week, but revenue doesn't move.\n\nWhy? Because according to the Theory of Constraints:\nIn any complex system, there is only ONE primary constraint limiting throughput at any given moment.\n\nOptimizing a non-constraint produces zero measurable results:\n- If your constraint is deal conversion at the proposal stage, generating 500 more marketing leads will not produce a single dollar of additional revenue. It will just waste rep time.\n- If your constraint is post-sale customer retention, doubling your sales headcount will only accelerate your churn rate.\n\nApply the Growth Constraint Triage:\n1. Demand Constraint: Are your reps' calendars under 50% booked with qualified buyers? -> Fix: Intent discovery and account selection.\n2. Conversion Constraint: Are qualified meetings failing to progress to proposal? -> Fix: Consultative discovery and problem-to-value translation.\n3. Velocity Constraint: Are deals stalling for 90+ days in procurement? -> Fix: Mutual Action Plans and pre-cleared legal packs.\n4. Retention Constraint: Are customers churning after Year 1? -> Fix: Delivery standardization and time-to-value acceleration.\n\nFind your single primary bottleneck. Focus 100% of your executive energy on solving it.\n\nWhat is the single biggest constraint limiting your revenue growth today?",
